+
+#### [nnUNet](https://github.com/MIC-DKFZ/nnUNet)
+> **Description:** nnU-Net is a self-configuring segmentation framework that automatically adapts U-Net pipelines to a dataset instead of forcing users to hand-tune architecture and preprocessing choices. The project’s core value is that it analyzes dataset properties, builds configurations, and delivers a strong out-of-the-box baseline across diverse biomedical segmentation tasks. It is one of the most cited and battle-tested open repositories in this space, making it a standard benchmark as well as a practical starting point. GitHub metadata: last commit date Mar 26, 2026, 8.2k stars, primary language Python, license Apache-2.0.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/MIC-DKFZ/nnUNet](https://github.com/MIC-DKFZ/nnUNet)
+- **Stars:** 8.2k ⭐
+- **Language:** Python
+- **License:** Apache-2.0
+- **Last Commit:** 2026-03-26
+- **Category:** segmentation, auto-configuration
+- **Best for:** high-quality biomedical image segmentation baselines
+
+---
+
+#### [MedSAM](https://github.com/bowang-lab/MedSAM)
+> **Description:** MedSAM adapts the Segment Anything concept to medical images and positions itself as an official medical-image segmentation implementation rather than a generic computer-vision fork. The repository focuses on promptable segmentation and practical inference scripts for healthcare imagery, making it attractive for teams that want modern segmentation interfaces on top of medical datasets. It is still research-heavy, but its adoption and star count reflect broad interest in foundation-model-style medical segmentation. GitHub metadata: last commit date May 7, 2025, 3.9k stars, primary language Jupyter Notebook, license Apache-2.0.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/bowang-lab/MedSAM](https://github.com/bowang-lab/MedSAM)
+- **Stars:** 3.9k ⭐
+- **Language:** Jupyter Notebook
+- **License:** Apache-2.0
+- **Last Commit:** 2025-05-07
+- **Category:** segmentation, foundation-models
+- **Best for:** prompt-based medical image segmentation
+
+---
+
+#### [TorchXRayVision](https://github.com/mlmed/torchxrayvision)
+> **Description:** TorchXRayVision provides a common interface for chest X-ray datasets, pretrained models, segmentation utilities, and autoencoders. Its README stresses standard preprocessing, consistent dataset access, and reusable pretrained models so researchers do not need to retrain everything from scratch for every study. That makes it especially practical for CXR classification, benchmarking, transfer learning, and exploratory work across NIH, CheXpert, MIMIC-CXR, PadChest, and related datasets. GitHub metadata: last commit date Sep 18, 2025, 1,083 stars, primary language Jupyter Notebook, license Apache-2.0.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/mlmed/torchxrayvision](https://github.com/mlmed/torchxrayvision)
+- **Stars:** 1,083 ⭐
+- **Language:** Jupyter Notebook
+- **License:** Apache-2.0
+- **Last Commit:** 2025-09-18
