+
+# Best AI Tools For Healthcare 2026
+
+[![Awesome](https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/sindresorhus/awesome@main/media/badge.svg)](https://github.com/sindresorhus/awesome)
+[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
+![Topics](https://img.shields.io/github/stars/GagnDeep/awesome-best-ai-tools-for-healthcare-2026?style=social)
+
+> This list curates the best AI tools for healthcare 2026 teams can actually inspect, fork, and extend because every project here is a public GitHub repository. It focuses on open-source medical imaging, pathology, clinical NLP, medical agents, and translational health tooling that can support research, internal platforms, and privacy-sensitive deployments.
+
+## Table of Contents
+- [TL;DR](#tldr)
+- [Why This List](#why-this-list)
+- [Open Source Tools](#open-source-tools)
+- [FAQ](#faq)
+- [Contributing](#contributing)
+- [License](#license)
+
+## TL;DR
+- **[Project MONAI](https://github.com/Project-MONAI/MONAI)** is the safest default if you need a broad healthcare-imaging stack with training, deployment, and annotation ecosystem support.
+- **[nnUNet](https://github.com/MIC-DKFZ/nnUNet)** remains one of the strongest open baselines for medical segmentation when you want reproducible results with minimal hand-tuning.
+- **[TorchXRayVision](https://github.com/mlmed/torchxrayvision)** is one of the easiest ways to work with chest X-ray models and datasets without rebuilding preprocessing pipelines.
+- **[medspacy](https://github.com/medspacy/medspacy)** is still one of the most practical open clinical NLP libraries for teams standardizing note processing.
+- **[DeepChem](https://github.com/deepchem/deepchem)** and **[scGPT](https://github.com/bowang-lab/scGPT)** are strong picks if your healthcare roadmap extends into drug discovery, genomics, or translational ML.
+
+## Why This List
+Open source matters in healthcare because teams need auditability, local deployment options, reproducibility, and the ability to adapt pipelines to institution-specific data. A flashy demo is not enough when protected health data, custom imaging modalities, pathology workflows, or regulated review processes are involved.
+
+This awesome list is intentionally narrow: every entry is a public GitHub repository, and proprietary SaaS products are excluded. For the best AI tools for healthcare 2026, that means favoring projects with transparent code, visible licenses, and recent GitHub activity over vendor marketing pages.
+
+## Open Source Tools
+
+### Medical Imaging & Segmentation
+
+#### [MONAI](https://github.com/Project-MONAI/MONAI)
+> **Description:** MONAI is a PyTorch-based healthcare-imaging framework built to cover the full lifecycle from preprocessing and augmentation to training and deployment. Its GitHub materials emphasize reproducibility, domain-specific transforms, AutoML support, GPU-accelerated I/O, and a shared foundation for research and production imaging workflows. It is one of the deepest open ecosystems in medical AI, with adjacent labeling, deployment, and model-zoo projects. GitHub metadata: last commit date Jan 5, 2026, 7,709 stars, primary language Python, license Apache-2.0.
+
