+> **Description:** STAMP is an end-to-end weakly supervised deep-learning workflow for discovering and evaluating image-based biomarkers from whole-slide pathology images. The README emphasizes reproducible, configurable pipelines, CLI-based operation, HPC support, and compatibility with multiple foundation models, which makes it useful for research groups that need a structured whole-slide workflow instead of isolated scripts. It is one of the cleaner open pathology repos for practical experimentation. GitHub metadata: last commit date Nov 28, 2025, 102 stars, primary language Python, license MIT.
